-- title:
--   Level independence of the specialisation family on J₁(Mp)
-- statement:
--   The setting is the following. A prime $p$, an integer $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, a valuation subring $Pl$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a $\{p\}$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ together with a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$, and a discrete valuation ring $A$ with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$. The field $K$ is an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$, required by `hK` to equal [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the image under coefficientwise extension of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$; it is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. The element $j \in K$ is, by `hj`, the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the $j$-invariant, and is assumed nonzero. Throughout, $X =$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChartModel A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L229) denotes the two-chart model, the pushout of the two spectra of the integral closures of $A[j]$ and $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$ glued along their common overring, and [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) its structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$; the residue field of $Pl$, written $\kappa$, is assumed algebraically closed of characteristic $p$ and an $A$-algebra.
--
--   The remaining data and hypotheses fall into the following groups, each of which is listed here by name with its content summarised.
--
--   Special fibre geometry: two proper, smooth of relative dimension one, geometrically integral curves $c_1 : C_1 \to \operatorname{Spec}\kappa$ and $c_2 : C_2 \to \operatorname{Spec}\kappa$, closed immersions $i_1, i_2$ of them over $\kappa$ into the base change $X_\kappa$, the hypothesis `hcover` that every point of $X_\kappa$ lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$, the hypothesis `hred` that the scheme-theoretic intersection $\mathrm{pullback}\,i_1\,i_2$ is reduced, and a natural number $n > 0$ equal to its cardinality (`hn`, `hn0`).
--
--   Sections: a section $\varepsilon$ of $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, sections $\varepsilon_1$, $\varepsilon_2$ of $c_1$, $c_2$, and `hε₁`, which says that $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ is the base change of $\varepsilon$ to $\kappa$.
--
--   Relative Picard data: a designation $D$ (a scheme $D.P$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ with a zero section), a witness `hrep` that $D$ represents the subfunctor of rigidified line bundles on $X$ along $\varepsilon$ cut out by the condition of being fibrewise algebraically equivalent to zero, hypotheses `hsm`, `hsep` that $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ is smooth and separated, the corresponding representability `hreps` for the base change to $\kappa$, the compatibility `hPk` of the two Poincaré bundles under base change, designations $D_1$, $D_2$ for $c_1$, $c_2$ with representability witnesses `hrep₁`, `hrep₂`, a morphism $\nu_2 : D_\kappa \to D_2$ over $\kappa$ and the hypothesis `hν₂` identifying, for every test object, the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of $D_2$ along $\nu_2$ with the rigidification along $\varepsilon_2$ of the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of $D_\kappa$ through $i_2$. The morphism [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) is assumed proper.
--
--   Generic fibre and geometric model: compatible algebra structures making $A \to L \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ a tower, the hypotheses `hsmL`, `hgiL` that $X_L$ is smooth of relative dimension one and geometrically integral, `hprL`, `hgcL` that $D_L \to \operatorname{Spec} L$ is proper and geometrically connected, a curve model $M_\eta$ of the function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182) over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with an isomorphism $e_\eta$ onto $X_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (`heη`), a nonemptiness assumption on the finite chart pulled back along $e_\eta$, the pinning hypothesis `hMηpin` that the function-field element attached by $M_\eta$ to each element $a$ of the finite chart algebra is the coefficientwise image of the Laurent expansion of $a$, and the equivariance `hgal` asserting that for Galois automorphisms $g$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ fixing $L$, translating a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point by $g$ translates the associated place by [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54) of $g$.
--
--   Hecke and Galois structure: the hypotheses `hin` and `hcomm` (the input data [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondInputsAll (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L58) and the commutation [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondCommuteBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L54) of the Hecke and diamond generators on $J_1(Mp)$), a semiring action of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ on $A$ compatible with $A \to L$ (`hΓA`), a special fibre geometry datum $G$ (abelian groups $G.J_{0s}$, $G.J_I$, $G.J_E$, a subgroup $G.\mathrm{torus}$, and a surjection $G.\mathrm{proj}$ onto $G.J_I \times G.J_E$ with kernel the torus), bijections `pts`, `ptsI`, `ptsE` of these groups with the $\kappa$-points of $D_\kappa$, $D_1$, $D_2$, the additivity hypotheses `hadd`, `haddI`, `haddE` on Poincaré pullbacks, and `hproj` expressing $G.\mathrm{proj}$ through $i_1$ and $\nu_2$.
--
--   Group-law and operator data on $D$: a bijection `gpts` between $J_1(Mp) = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182) and the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of $D$, an assignment $\varphi$ of endomorphisms of $D$ to elements of the Hecke algebra [`ModularCurve.HeckeAlgOne`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L16), a semilinear assignment $\tau$ for $s \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$, and the hypotheses `hφmul` (additivity of $\varphi(t)$ for the relative group law), `hφpts` (compatibility of $\varphi$ with the Hecke module structure through `gpts`), `hτ1`, `hτmul`, `hτφ` (the cocycle identities for $\tau$ and its commutation with $\varphi$), `hgadd` (additivity of `gpts`) and `hτpts` (Galois equivariance of `gpts`).
--
--   Abel–Jacobi data: the representability `hDL` over $L$, a morphism `ajL` from $X_L$ to $D_L$, a comparison morphism `kL` between the two base changes of $X$, a morphism `ajbar` from $M_\eta.C$ to $D.P$, a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point `εbar` of $M_\eta.C$, and the hypotheses `hPL`, `hajLε`, `hajL`, `hkL₁`, `hkL₂`, `hajbar`, `hajbar_over`, `hεbar`, `hεbar_aj`, `hpts_aj` which fix `ajL` as the Abel–Jacobi map normalised at $\varepsilon$, identify `ajbar` with its geometric avatar, and assert that for $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x$ and $s$ of $M_\eta.C$ with $s$ the reduction of $\varepsilon$ the divisor class of $[x] - [s]$ maps under `gpts` to $x$ followed by `ajbar`.
--
--   Special fibre operators: a datum $O$ of type [`ModularCurve.JOneP.NeronSpecialFibreOpsV3 G`](def/ModularCurve_JOnePOpsV3.html#L13) (Hecke operators, two families of diamond operators, an Atkin–Lehner involution, an inertia action, and their commutation relations) and the hypothesis `hO` with four clauses matching, through `pts` and the first projection, the operators $O.\mathrm{hecke}\,\ell$, $O.\mathrm{diamondP}\,b$, $O.\mathrm{diamondN}\,d$ and $O.\mathrm{inertia}\,b$ with $\varphi$ of the corresponding Hecke and diamond generators and with $\tau(s)$ for $s$ acting on $\zeta$ by $\zeta \mapsto \zeta^{b}$.
--
--   Local data at $Pl$: `hPl` that $Pl$ lies over $p$, a ring map $\rho : A \to Pl$ compatible with $A \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (`hρ`) and with the residue map (`hAlgκ`).
--
--   The hypothesis `hF3` is the $\mathcal{O}_I$-points statement: for every subgroup $I$ of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ contained in the inertia subgroup at $Pl$, fixing all $p$-th roots of unity, and of finite index in that inertia subgroup, writing $\mathcal{O}_I = Pl \cap \overline{\mathbb{Q}}^{I}$, there exist a ring map $\rho_I : A \to \mathcal{O}_I$ lifting $A \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that, with $\mathrm{dom}$ the set of $x \in J_1(Mp)$ whose point `gpts x` factors through $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}_I$: every element of $\mathrm{dom}$ is fixed by $I$; such factorisations are unique; $\mathrm{dom}$ contains $0$ and is closed under differences; for $n > 0$ prime to $p$ the reduction map is injective on $n$-torsion $\mathcal{O}_I$-points and surjective onto $n$-torsion $\kappa$-points; and $\mathrm{dom}$ is stable under any Frobenius element at $Pl$ normalising $I$.
--
--   Néron model data: a scheme $\mathcal{A}$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ with a closed immersion $\iota$ into $D.P$ over $A$, and the hypothesis `h𝒜` asserting that $\iota$ is a closed immersion, $\mathcal{A} \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ is proper and smooth with connected geometric fibres, that $\mathcal{A}$ is closed under the unit, multiplication and inversion of the relative group law on $D$, that the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of $\mathcal{A}$ cut out exactly [`ModularCurve.normFreePartAt (M * p) p`](def/ModularCurve_X1PrimitiveSpecializationAtP.html#L29) inside $J_1(Mp)$ through `gpts`, and that $\mathcal{A}$ is stable under all $\varphi(t)$. The hypothesis `hF10` asserts that any point of $D_\kappa$ with values in a $\kappa$-algebra $T'$ which lifts to $\mathcal{A}$ is killed by $\varphi$ of the sum over $b \in (\mathbb{Z}/p)^\times$ of the diamond generators [`ModularCurve.diamondGen`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L20) at the integers prescribed by the Chinese remainder isomorphism.
--
--   Igusa identification of the special fibre: an integral weight-one form $w$ of level $M$ over $\kappa$, two curve models $\mathrm{Mdl}_1$, $\mathrm{Mdl}_2$ of the Igusa function field [`ModularCurve.igusaFunctionFieldX1C κ M w`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L35) with isomorphisms $e_1 : \mathrm{Mdl}_1.C \cong C_1$, $e_2 : \mathrm{Mdl}_2.C \cong C_2$ over $\kappa$ (`he₁`, `he₂`), a nonemptiness assumption on the relevant chart of $C_1$, the $q$-expansion pinning `hgauss₁` computing, for chart elements written as quotients of power series, the Laurent expansion on $\mathrm{Mdl}_1$ as the reduction of that quotient, the hypothesis `hεC₂` that the reduction of $\varepsilon$ avoids $C_2$, the hypothesis `hεgal` that $\varepsilon$ is equivariant for any automorphism of the two-chart model inducing a prescribed Galois action on the chart algebra, and `hPTS` that `pts` is additive and sends $0$ to the unit.
--
--   Raynaud-type description: a finite set `nodesIg` of pairs of places of the Igusa function field, isomorphisms $\Psi : G.J_{0s} \cong \mathrm{GluedPic}^0$ of that function field with gluing set `nodesIg`, and $\theta_1, \theta_2$ from $G.J_I$, $G.J_E$ to $\mathrm{Pic}^0$, together with the hypothesis `hF4c`: `nodesIg` consists exactly of the pairs of places cut out by the $\kappa$-points of $\mathrm{pullback}\,i_1\,i_2$, has cardinality $n$, has injective first and second projections, $\Psi$ is compatible with $G.\mathrm{proj}$ and the pair $(\theta_1,\theta_2)$, the image of $G.\mathrm{torus}$ under $\Psi$ is the range of the node-unit homomorphism, and $\theta_1$, $\theta_2$ are given by the Abel–Jacobi recipe $[x] - [\varepsilon_i]$. The datum `frobT` is a semilinear automorphism of the Igusa function field over $\kappa$ raising each Laurent coefficient to the $p$-th power (`hfrobT`).
--
--   The specialisation family: for each admissible $I$ as in `hF3` (contained in the inertia subgroup at $Pl$, fixing $\mu_p$, of finite index there) an additive subgroup $\mathrm{dom}\mathcal{D}(I)$ of $J_1(Mp)$ and an additive map $\mathrm{sp}\mathcal{D}(I)$ from it to $\mathrm{GluedPic}^0$, subject to the interface `hIFm`: $y$ lies in $\mathrm{dom}\mathcal{D}(I)$ if and only if `gpts y` factors through $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}_I$ via the ring map chosen in `hF3`; and for such $y$, any factorisation $z$ and any $\kappa$-point $u$ of $D_\kappa$ whose associated morphism to $D.P$ is the reduction of $z$ along $\mathcal{O}_I \to \kappa$, one has $\mathrm{sp}\mathcal{D}(I)(y) = \Psi(\mathrm{pts}^{-1}(u))$.
--
--   The conclusion is the conjunction of two statements, each quantified over two admissible subgroups $I$ and $J$ (each contained in the inertia subgroup at $Pl$, fixing all $p$-th roots of unity, of finite index in that inertia subgroup) with $J \le I$.
--
--   First, for every $y \in J_1(Mp)$ and every factorisation $z$ of `gpts y` through $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}_I$ (over the ring map chosen by `hF3` at $I$), with `hz` the identity $(\mathrm{gpts}\,y) = \operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusion $\mathcal{O}_I \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ followed by $z$: there are an inclusion $\mathcal{O}_I \le \mathcal{O}_J$ of subrings of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and a point $z_J$ of $D.P$ over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the ring map chosen by `hF3` at $J$, such that $z_J$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusion $\mathcal{O}_I \le \mathcal{O}_J$ followed by $z$; `gpts y` equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusion $\mathcal{O}_J \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ followed by $z_J$; and the reduction of $z_J$ along $\mathcal{O}_J \to \kappa$ coincides with the reduction of $z$ along $\mathcal{O}_I \to \kappa$ (both residue maps being induced by $\mathcal{O}_\bullet \le Pl$ followed by the residue map of $Pl$).
--
--   Second, for every $y$ belonging to $\mathrm{dom}\mathcal{D}(I)$ there is a proof that $y$ belongs to $\mathrm{dom}\mathcal{D}(J)$, and for it $\mathrm{sp}\mathcal{D}(J)(y) = \mathrm{sp}\mathcal{D}(I)(y)$.
--
--   This is the change-of-level step for the specialisation maps attached to the norm-free part of $J_1(Mp)$ at $p$: an integral point of the relative Picard scheme defined over the inertia-fixed ring $\mathcal{O}_I$ is also defined over the smaller ring $\mathcal{O}_J$ for $J \le I$, with unchanged reduction, so that the resulting map to the glued $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the two Igusa components does not depend on the chosen level $I$. It supplies the level-independence hypothesis used by [`ModularCurve.exists_qExpSemistableSpecializationPinnedV3_family_normFreePart_and_diamond_of_dvd_of_not_sq_dvd_of_le_div`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_qExpSemistableSpecializationPinnedV3_family_normFreePart_and_diamond_of_dvd_of_not_sq_dvd_of_le_div).
